{"reference":"Psalms 79","book":"Psalms","chapter":79,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"A communal lament","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"One disputed reading understands Psalm 79 as a communal psalm preserving the memory of sanctuary destruction and the Babylonian exile. The prayer’s repeated “we” and its concern for Jerusalem, the temple, and the people’s suffering are read within that shared experience of devastation and appeal for deliverance.","verse_refs":["Psalms 79:1-13"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_079_55d56c67cf4921d05b9bf86a"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}